------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code and derivation status (as of the v0.0.1 skeleton milestone)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NO third-party source code has been copied or directly derived into this
repository at this milestone. The skeleton was written from scratch following
the Zotero 7/9 bootstrapped-plugin lifecycle documented at:

  https://www.zotero.org/support/dev/zotero_7_for_developers

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Planned future derivation: ZotMoov
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The design document `zot-link_设计与ZotMoov分析_2026-06-16.md` identifies the
following ZotMoov (https://github.com/wileyyugioh/zotmoov, GPL-3.0) mechanisms
as references / candidates for porting into later milestones:

  1. The imported-to-linked attachment conversion sequence in
     `02-zotmoov.js` (clone -> set LINK_MODE_LINKED_FILE -> save -> copy file
     -> move child items -> erase original). [Design doc §4.3]
  2. The Notifier registration pattern in `01-zotmoov-notify-callback.js`.
  3. The right-click / Tools menu registration patterns in
     `03-zotmoov-menus*.js`.

When any of the above is ported, this NOTICE will be updated to:

  - State which ZotMoov file(s) and which revision were referenced.
  - State whether the port is verbatim copy, line-by-line adaptation, or
     reimplementation guided by the original.
  - Continue to license the derivative under GPL-3.0-only.

ZotMoov's `00-zotmoov-wildcard.js` and `00-zotmoov-command-parser.js` are
NOT planned for use; zot-link's path scheme is a fixed `_items/{KEY}/...`
structure rather than user-configurable wildcards.
